<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco I Gattilusio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1384</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco I <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gattilusio">Gattilusio</a> was a Genoese adventurer who helped the Byzantine emperor John V Palaiologos regain his throne from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a> in 1354. In reward he received the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a> and the hand of John V's sister Maria, founding the Gattilusio lordship of Lesbos. He ruled from Mytilene until he was killed in an earthquake in 1384.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-i-gattilusio.jpg" alt="Francesco I Gattilusio" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown 14th century mint master · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denaro_of_Francesco_I_Gattilusio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
